;; fault-jal-mis.expected.sexp — the expected observations for `fault-jal-mis.s` (P2-SCALAR.3).
;; Validate with:
;;   python3 scripts/check_sexp_schema.py fault-jal-mis.expected.sexp schema/expectations.sexp

(comment "rv64gc note (P4-SYSTEM.2 slice f): the IALIGN=16 divergence class — mirrored_from rv64i-lab-v0, whose IALIGN=32 makes the 2-mod-4 target fault. Under D-IALIGN-16 (RVI-C 27.1) that target is LEGAL, so the link write lands (x5 <- pc+4) and the rv64i document's never_written x5 does not transfer. The terminal fetch at the 2-mod-4 target ends the recorded trace (the composition declares C a slot; 16-bit decode lands with it).")
(comment "fault-jal-mis.expected.sexp — the expected observations for `fault-jal-mis.s`." "" "⛔ EVERY VALUE HERE WAS DERIVED FROM THE PINNED SPECIFICATION PROSE BEFORE THE PROGRAM WAS RUN" "(EVD-05). The trap step is last: a contained trap stops the laboratory run. ⭐ x5 must NEVER" "be written: an instruction that raises a synchronous exception retires no architectural write —" "the DEFECT-B pin (the model once wrote the link before trapping; both references suppress it," "measured).")
(expectations (program "fault-jal-mis.s") (entry "0x80000000") (instructions 2) (step (n 0) (insn "addi x1, x0, 1") (writes (write (reg "x1") (value "0x0000000000000001"))) (derivation "An ordinary write, so the run has a step before the trap and the trap's position is observable.") (source "RVI-RV32I §1.1.4")) (step (n 1) (insn "jal x5, 2") (writes (write (reg "x5") (value "0x0000000080000008"))) (derivation "The target is 0x80000004 + 2 = 0x80000006, not 4-byte aligned under IALIGN=32, so the jump raises instruction-address-misaligned ON THE JUMP with tval = the target value, and the link write to x5 is SUPPRESSED — an instruction that raises a synchronous exception retires no write. Measured on both references: cause 0x00, tval 0x0000000080000006, and neither writes x5.") (source "RVI-RV32I §1.1.5 (D-IALIGN); §1.1.5.2 (D-MISALIGN-REPORT: raised on the jump, tval = the target)")))
